WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.010
A car pulls in with a problem.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.430
Every shop before this one kept its own separate paper trail.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.117
Type anything you've got:

00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:12.930
the plate, the VIN, even just the owner's name,

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.290
and Altobay starts searching right away.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.710
It doesn't just check your own records.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.909
It reaches into every shop this car has ever visited,

00:00:23.909 --> 00:00:24.690
all at once.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.501
In seconds, the full history drops in:

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:32.170
five visits, five different outcomes,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.190
every one of them logged by a shop that isn't yours.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.804
Tap into any visit and the record opens up:

00:00:40.804 --> 00:00:42.490
what was actually serviced,

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.354
what the mechanic noted, which parts were used,

00:00:45.354 --> 00:00:47.390
and what it's likely to need next.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.050
Nothing here comes from guesswork.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.355
Every visit is color-coded the moment it loads:

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.510
done, in progress, or waiting,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.650
so nothing about this car's condition is a surprise.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:04.880
One search.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.299
A car's entire history, wherever it happened.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:10.870
This is Altobay.
